      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0768",
      "reading_order": 888,
      "section": "Connection of sealing liquid for mechanical seals",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.004049999999985,
        "t": 402.68185,
        "r": 167.52405,
        "b": 391.44185
      },
      "content": "Seal lubrication is required"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0769",
      "reading_order": 889,
      "section": "Connection of sealing liquid for mechanical seals",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 144.00401,
        "t": 388.16186,
        "r": 557.5940400000004,
        "b": 364.92186
      },
      "content": "Seal faces must have liquid film between them for proper lubrication. Locate the taps using the illustrations shipped with the seal."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0770",
      "reading_order": 890,
      "section": "Seal flushing methods",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 54.00400999999998,
        "t": 358.16186,
        "r": 147.89400999999998,
        "b": 346.92186
      },
      "content": "Seal flushing methods",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0771",
      "reading_order": 891,
      "section": "Seal flushing methods",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 144.00401999999997,
        "t": 346.16186,
        "r": 378.92402000000004,
        "b": 334.92186
      },
      "content": "You can use these methods in order to flush or cool the seal:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "tbl_0044",
      "reading_order": 892,
      "section": "Seal flushing methods",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 142.8123321533203,
        "t": 335.1068115234375,
        "r": 558.9703369140625,
        "b": 211.70953369140625
      },
      "markdown": "| Method         | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Product flush  | Run the piping so that the pump pushes the pumped fluid from the casing and injects it into the seal gland. If necessary, an external heat exchanger cools the pumped fluid before it enters the seal gland.                                                                         |\n| External flush | Run the piping so that the pump injects a clean, cool, compatible liquid directly into the seal gland. The pressure of the flushing liquid must be 5 to 15 psi (0.35 to 1.01 kg/cm 2 ) greater than the seal chamber pressure. The injection rate must be 0.5 to 2 gpm (2 to 8 lpm). |\n| Other          | You can use other methods that employ multiple gland or seal chamber connections. Refer to the mechanical seal reference drawing and piping diagrams.                                                                                                                                |"
    },
